('Agent Plugins 1.0','good','portable tooling','https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-12-agent-plugins-1-0-in-vs-code-copilot-cli-and-the-copilot-app/','A plugin can be built once and used across VS Code, Copilot CLI, the Copilot SDK, and the Copilot app.','Portability shifts reuse from prompt text to packaged tools, skills, and policy-aware interfaces.','Package recurring Buildn research or reporting actions as a portable plugin contract.','Compatibility does not guarantee identical permissions or behavior on every host.','Write one plugin manifest with explicit inputs, outputs, and side effects.'),
('Headless plan + autopilot','good','execution','https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-13-github-copilot-weekly-releases-august-10/','Copilot CLI can create a plan and implement it headlessly, while centralized task management handles subagents and queued work.','The useful primitive is a visible plan boundary before autonomous execution.','Require plan artifacts before agents modify client repositories or publish reports.','Autopilot remains sensitive to repository context and test quality.','Compare planned versus changed files on five low-risk tasks.'),
('Non-destructive rewind','good','recovery','https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-13-github-copilot-weekly-releases-august-10/','The CLI can restore agent changes without requiring Git or discarding user edits.','Recovery is a prerequisite for safe experimentation with higher autonomy.','Mirror the idea in Buildn workspaces: isolate agent edits and expose a reversible checkpoint.','Rewind semantics must be tested around generated files, renames, and concurrent edits.','Define a reversible-change contract and test it with fixtures.'),
('Copilot memory in JetBrains','warn','continuity','https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-11-copilot-memory-and-ollama-in-github-copilot-for-jetbrains/','JetBrains sessions can preserve project details and preferences across agent chats.','Cross-session memory reduces repeated setup but raises provenance and staleness questions.','Use explicit project memory files rather than invisible personalization for client work.','Memory may preserve wrong assumptions unless users can inspect and clear it.','Adopt a visible memory ledger with source, owner, and expiry.'),
